# Platform delivery

When implementing work that touches **both** the shared seam (`core/`) **and** one or more clients (`apps/android`, `apps/web`, later `apps/ios`):

1. Follow the project skill `platform-delivery` (core first → platforms → tests).
2. Tests are **required** (core unit; Android emulator smoke; web build when web changed). Empty `adb devices` → start the AVD via `android-emulator`. If a gate cannot run: **stop and ask**. No skips.
3. Overview: [docs/conventions/agent-dev-environment.md](../../docs/conventions/agent-dev-environment.md).

Single-area edits (only core, only one app, or docs-only) do not require the full fan-out.
